  "_comment": "FreeScout modules the package's Modules tab can install. Each entry is a public GitHub repository holding a module (module.json at the root, or under `path`), ideally with tagged releases (vX.Y.Z; without releases the default branch is used). The setup container reads module.json for the name, alias, description, logo, provider (folder name) and requirements, and the latest release for the version. Fields: repo (owner/name), path (folder inside the repository holding module.json, if not the root), note (shown on the card), requires (modules this one needs: alias, name, url, optional), composer_install (true: run `composer install` inside the module's folder before activating, for a module that ships its own composer.json and loads its own vendor/autoload.php). To add your own without rebuilding the package, put a file like this at modules.json in the freescout shared folder; its entries are added to these.",
